title: 'chain-spec-builder: manage the boot nodes of a chain spec'
doc:
- audience: [Node Dev, Node Operator]
  description: |-
    `chain-spec-builder` can now manage the boot nodes of a chain specification. The new
    `bootnodes` command group operates on an existing chain spec, in both plain and raw format,
    through its `add`, `remove` and `list` subcommands, and the `create` command takes a new
    `--bootnodes` argument. The given addresses are validated: they must be multiaddresses
    containing the peer id of the node.

    `bootnodes add` appends to the existing list, skipping the addresses that are already stored,
    and `bootnodes remove` ignores the addresses that are not stored, so both can be safely
    repeated. When no address is given in the command line they prompt for the addresses to
    operate on: `add` reads them one per line, and `remove` displays the stored addresses as a
    numbered list and reads the numbers to remove. `bootnodes remove --all` removes all of them
    without prompting.
crates:
- name: staging-chain-spec-builder
  bump: minor
- name: sc-chain-spec
  bump: minor
